    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 17th with a clear emphasis on exploiting stolen base opportunities against slow-working pitchers. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.25) stands as our premier play today; despite a lower lineup slot, his efficiency is supercharged by a highly favorable matchup against Fedde and a defensive profile that remains secondary to his elite sprint speed against a favorable SP delivery. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (71.68) commands a \"Strong\" start, benefiting from a 13% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages and a stolen base threat against a pitcher delivery that yields an 87% success rate. While **Junior Caminero** (63.35) and **Carson Benge** (63.27) also clear the 60-point mark comfortably, our core remains anchored by their ability to manufacture runs in high-leverage spots despite the occasional volatility of their respective opponents.\n\nRegarding our bench decisions, **Chase Meidroth** (49.85) was the most difficult exclusion, finishing as our highest-ranked bench player. While his projection remains respectable, he lacked the explosive \"breakout\" variables found in our OF and UTIL slots, ultimately falling short due to a neutral park factor and a lack of the stolen base upside that we prioritize for our 5x5 needs. Meanwhile, **Dillon Dingler** (39.99) was correctly benched as he dipped below our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold, largely due to a harsh dynamic platoon penalty against Gausman.\n\nOwners should exercise caution regarding the top of our order: **Trea Turner** (48.87) and **Kyle Schwarber** (47.62) face an elite challenge today in Skenes. Their scores are heavily dampened by the SP\u2019s dominant profile (-19% skill penalty), and while their order placement keeps them in the lineup, they carry significant risk of blanking in the HR and RBI categories. Ensure all lineups are locked before first pitch, as the absence of **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Caleb Durbin** from today's active rotation leaves no room for error if late lineup changes impact our depth.",
